# /write-prd (Cursor)

Turn an approved Plan Mode conversation into a PRD that `sdlc-workflow decompose` can parse on the first try.

1. Copy `rosetta_docs/product/TEMPLATE.md` verbatim as the starting point — do not write PRD structure from memory. Match its heading text and numbering exactly (`### 1.2 Goals`, `### 1.3 Non-Goals`, `### 1.4 Acceptance Criteria`) and its `## N. Rollout & Phases` numbered-phase format (a "Phase \<N\>" reference followed by a dash and a title).
2. Fill in every section from the approved plan. Do not invent `forbiddenSurfaces` labels later at decompose/spec time that aren't already defined in the target repo's `.sdlc/surfaces.json` — check that file first if the plan touches a sensitive surface.
3. Before running `decompose` (which costs an LLM call), validate the PRD parses cleanly and for free: `sdlc-workflow prd-lint --prd <PRD-ID> --docs-dir <path-to-docs-dir>`. Fix any `PRD_MALFORMED` error it reports before proceeding.
4. Only after `prd-lint` passes, run `sdlc-workflow decompose --prd <PRD-ID> --repo <target-repo>` to generate the Draft spec and stop at the human gate.

The parser fails loudly and specifically now (it used to silently return empty sections on a heading mismatch) — `prd-lint` exists precisely so that loud failure happens before the LLM call, not after.
